Job Description 
 Build the future with us
 Are you passionate about designing high-performing technology solutions and eager to contribute to the purpose of a company that aims to help its clients feel confident and secure about their future?
 As a Senior Software Designer , you will play a key role in the design and evolution of innovative, robust and reusable software solutions, while providing technical leadership to teams.
 This position is a great opportunity to showcase your skills and fully realize your potential within a caring and trustworthy company. Here, people and their development are at the heart of our priorities, fostering an environment that encourages collaboration and innovation.
 What you’ll accomplish with us 
 As a Principal Software Designer, you’ll be at the core of our mission. Here are the main responsibilities:
 Design high-performing, innovative and reusable software solutions and components in distributed architecture and microservices environments;
 Contribute to the design, integration and deployment of artificial intelligence capabilities within business solutions, in collaboration with the appropriate specialists;
 Work closely with architects to translate architectural direction into concrete and detailed software solutions, particularly for REST API integration and the orchestration of complex business processes;
 Act as a technical leader, maintain design integrity, oversee implementation, and mentor internal and external resources;
 Collaborate with multiple teams responsible for interdependent systems in an environment combining modern and legacy systems;
 Evolve the practices, tools and methods within the discipline while staying current with technology trends;
 Ensure compliance with standards and maintain comprehensive, up-to-date technical documentation;
 Support the configuration, deployment, observability and operationalization of solutions;
 Promote best practices in DevOps, observability, security and AI-assisted development.
 What could accelerate your success in this role 
 We’re looking for someone who:
 Holds a bachelor’s degree in computer science or another relevant field of study at an equivalent level;
 Has more than 10 years of experience in information technology, including at least 5 years in IT software solution design;
 Is recognized for their technical leadership and ability to effectively communicate and explain complex issues, solve problems, and guide decision-making in collaboration with various stakeholders;
 Has extensive expertise in software design within distributed and microservices architectures, as well as in the design and integration of REST APIs;
 Has strong knowledge of Agile and Lean methodologies, continuous deployment concepts and tools, and DevOps practices;
 Has strong knowledge of observability and logging best practices, as well as error and vulnerability detection;
 Has a very good understanding of regulatory requirements, information security frameworks such as NIST and ISO 27001, and security best practices;
 Has a good understanding of data management and integration, database development, data warehousing, data modelling and data analysis;
 Has experience with data-related technologies and languages, including SQL, PL/SQL, NoSQL and Snowflake, as well as Master Data Management and Reference Data Management solutions (MDM and RDM);
 Has strong knowledge of or relevant experience with .NET 10, SQL Server, Kafka, Kubernetes and Microsoft Azure, as well as Azure DevOps, Visual Studio, Visual Studio Code, GitHub Copilot, Git, Postman, SQL Server Management Studio and Dynatrace;
 Knowledge of Terraform and Camunda is considered an asset;
 Professional information security certifications such as CISSP, CRISC, CISA, CGEIT or COBIT are considered assets;
 Knowledge of the insurance and financial services industry is considered an asset;
 Demonstrates an excellent ability to understand the nuances and complexities of a sophisticated business domain;
 Has an advanced level of French and an intermediate level of English proficiency, as the role involves weekly collaboration by videoconference and email with internal English-speaking colleagues.
 Why you’ll love working with us 
 A work environment where learning and development merge with a collective pursuit of excellence;
 AI is in everyone's hands, empowering you to increase your personal effectiveness while supporting the organization's growth;
 A healthy, safe, fair, and inclusive environment where potential can be freely expressed and developed;
 The opportunity to work in a hybrid environment, supported by flexibility and access to inspiring and innovative workspaces.
 Competitive Benefits 
 Flexible group insurance plans;
 Competitive retirement savings plan;
 Employee share purchase plan;
 Vacation program, wellness days, and personal development days;
 Telemedicine services;
 Employee and Family Assistance Program (EFAP);
 Ergonomic furniture program;
 Performance bonus;
 Discounts on iA products;
 And much more!
 Apply now and get ahead of your career, where your talent really belongs!
 Still unsure about applying?
 At iA, we believe in potential and value diverse experiences. If this role inspires you, go ahead and apply: your place might be with us, and we want to get to know you!
